//@ run-pass
//@ timeout: 300
//@ expect-stdout-contains: CIRC28_DRUG_ARIPIPRAZOLE_PASS
//
// Aripiprazole (oral tablet) + dehydro-aripiprazole on the circ28 drug record, coupled by circ28_metab.sio
// (stdlib/darwin_pbpk/circ28_drug_aripiprazole.sio; parameter table, pooled observables and sources in its
// header). CYP2D6 extensive metaboliser (EM) unless stated; 73 kg reference male.
//
// S0 INPUT-CONSISTENCY CHECK (printed first, before any run): V_ss ln2 / CL against the terminal half-life.
//   Pooled CL 3.437 L/h (k = 4, u 0.297), V_ss 357.7 L (k = 1): V_ss ln2/CL = 72.1 h (80.9 h with the IV
//   clearance of the SmPC alone). Terminal half-life: label 75 h; pooled over five reports 63.7 h (between-study
//   SD 7.1, u 3.2). A terminal half-life can never be shorter than V_ss ln2/CL, so the inputs are INCONSISTENT
//   against the pooled half-life (ratio 1.13) and leave almost no room for a distribution phase against the
//   label's 75 h (ratio 0.96). The only IV volume is the label's (one study, n = 18, values not in the abstract
//   of Boulton 2008); the oral studies give V_z = CL t/ln2 of 246-377 L, which bound V_ss from above in each of
//   them. Nothing is added to the structure for this: the model half-life must come out above 72 h, and row V5b
//   is expected to fail for that reason.
//
// FITTED, hence NOT validations (one observable per fitted parameter):
//   P Kp scalar -> V_ss 357.7 L;  P total hepatic intrinsic clearance -> pooled CL;  P fa -> pooled F 0.86;
//   f2D6 -> pooled PM/EM parent exposure ratio 1.677 (k = 3);  fm -> pooled steady-state M/P ratio 0.417 (k = 5);
//   M hepatic intrinsic clearance -> pooled terminal half-life of M 100.65 h (k = 2).
//   ASSUMED, not fitted: r = phi_A/phi_D = 1 (both enzymes dehydrogenate with the same share); Kp scalar of M =
//   Kp scalar of P; B:P of M = B:P of P; no gut-wall metabolism; the non-2D6 hepatic clearance is CYP3A4 in the
//   inhibitor / inducer what-ifs. MEASURED, not fitted: ka 1.67 /h (so Tmax is a validation row), cl_renal.
//   Rows marked (c) use a study that is inside a pool: consistency checks, not independent tests.
//
// CRITERIA, fixed before the runs: an observation with an SD (inter-individual, or between-study for a pool):
//   |z| <= 2; an observation with no spread: within a factor 1.5; an exposure RATIO (phenotype or interaction):
//   within a factor 1.25; "steady state within 14 days": trough at day 14 >= 0.90 of the steady-state trough.
//
// PREDICTIONS WRITTEN BEFORE THE FIRST KERNEL RUN. The closed-form numbers (no kernel run) were computed in a
// scratch program first and are disclosed as seen: kpsc 0.2082, total hepatic intrinsic clearance 364.7 L/h,
// Eh 0.0566, fa 0.9116, AUCinf 2502 ng h/mL per 10 mg, V_ss,M 414.9 L, CL_M 2.857 L/h, fm 0.345, f2D6 0.404,
// PM V_ss ln2/CL 118.2 h, ketoconazole 2.00, quinidine 1.677, carbamazepine 0.207, Rodgers-Rowland scalar 1 for
// M: V_ss 1980 L, CL_M 13.6 L/h, fm 1.65 (infeasible). Kernel-dependent numbers below are HAND ESTIMATES with a
// range (tissue volumes x Kp against flows: everything but adipose equilibrates within ~2 h, adipose holds
// 254 of 358 L and fills with a time constant of ~21 h).
//   V1  Cmax 10 mg                  65 ng/mL (55-80)   obs 50.6 +/- 15.5 (Koller 2020, n 24) (c)       PASS
//   V1b Cmax 10 mg vs Li 2025        same               obs 48 +/- 13 (ODT, 64 kg Chinese, n 30)        PASS
//   V1c Cmax 6 mg                   39 ng/mL           obs 31.0 (Kubo 2007, Japanese, no SD)           PASS (fold 1.26)
//   V2  Tmax                        2.0 h (1.5-3)      obs pooled 4.27 h, SD 0.83 (label 3-5 h)        FAIL (too early:
//                                   the flow-limited kernel distributes within the absorption time)
//   V3  AUC0-24, 10 mg              1000 (850-1150)    obs 724.9 +/- 236.5 ng h/mL (Koller) (c)        PASS (z ~ +1.2)
//   V4  AUC0-72, 10 mg              1950 (1750-2150)   obs 1745 +/- 405 (Li 2025)                      PASS
//   V5  terminal t1/2 P             78 h (74-84)       obs 75 h (label, no SD)                         PASS
//   V5b terminal t1/2 P vs pool     same               obs 63.7 h, between-study SD 7.1 (k = 5)        FAIL (z ~ +2.0, marginal;
//                                                                                                     forced by S0)
//   V5c apparent t1/2 P, 96-240 h   ~75 h              obs 66.1 +/- 24.6 (Koller: last sample 240 h)   PASS
//   V6  Cmax after dose 5 (10 mg/d) 142 (125-160)      obs 138.0 +/- 45.9 (Koller) (c)                 PASS
//   V6b Cmax dose 5 / dose 1        2.15               obs 2.73 = 138.0/50.6 (ratio of means)          PASS at 1.5 (fold 0.79)
//   V7  P trough,ss per mg/day      8.9 ng/mL/mg       obs 9.0 +/- 2.9 (Suzuki 2011, Japanese, n 27)   PASS
//   V7b P average,ss per mg/day     10.4 (closed form) obs 11.8 = 26.3 nM/mg (Hendset 2007 EM median)  PASS at 1.5
//   V8  P trough day 14 / ss        0.95               label: steady state within 14 days              PASS
//   V8b M trough day 14 / ss        0.73               same                                            FAIL (two-step chain,
//                                                                                                     72 h then 100 h)
//   V9  M AUC0-24 day 1, 10 mg      30 (20-40)         obs 77.4 +/- 43.9 (Koller)                      PASS only through the SD (z ~ -1.1)
//   V9b M Cmax after dose 5         12 (9-16)          obs 34.9 +/- 8.5 (Koller) (c)                   FAIL (z ~ -2.7): a metabolite
//                                   with a 100 h half-life cannot reach a quarter of the parent in five days when
//                                   its steady-state ratio is 0.42. See the IDENTIFIABILITY diagnosis D1.
//   V10 M trough,ss per mg/day      4.2                obs 4.9 +/- 1.6 (Suzuki 2011) (c)               PASS
//   V11 PM terminal t1/2 P          128 h (120-136)    obs 146 h (label, no SD)                        PASS
//   V11b PM/EM t1/2 ratio           1.64               obs 1.947 = 146/75 (label)                      PASS at 1.25 (fold 0.84)
//   V12 PM/EM metabolite exposure   1.00 (r = 1)       obs 0.685 pooled (label 0.70, Belmonte 0.67)    FAIL (fold 1.46): the TEST of
//                                                                                                     the assumption r = 1
//   V13 PM/EM active moiety         1.48               obs 1.585, between-study SD 0.100 (k = 4)       PASS (z ~ -1.1)
//   V14 ketoconazole what-if        2.00               obs 1.63 (label and SmPC)                       PASS at 1.25 (fold 1.23, marginal)
//       hepatic non-2D6 clearance x 0.16 (LABELLED WHAT-IF: 0.16 = 1/6.3, the quetiapine CL/F change with
//       ketoconazole 200 mg/d, Grimm 2006, abstract; assumes quetiapine is cleared by CYP3A4 only, gut included)
//   V15 quinidine what-if           1.677 (= PM)       obs 2.095 (label +112 %, SmPC +107 %)           FAIL at 1.25 (fold 0.80)
//       CYP2D6 part x 0 (complete inhibition); by construction equal to the fitted PM ratio
//   V16 carbamazepine what-if       0.207              obs 0.287 (label 0.30, SmPC 0.27, Citrome 0.29) FAIL at 1.25 (fold 0.72)
//       hepatic non-2D6 clearance x 7.5 (LABELLED WHAT-IF: quetiapine CL/F 7.5-fold with carbamazepine, Grimm 2006)
//   V17 unabsorbed fraction 1 - fa  0.088              label: ~18 % of the dose unchanged in faeces    PASS (bound: <= 0.18)
//   V18 dose linearity 5-30 mg      exact (linear model) label: linear 5-30 mg                         PASS (identity)
//   BUDGET steady-state active-moiety trough at 15 mg/day: 198 ng/mL, relative u ~9.5 %; shares: pooled CL ~85 %,
//       M/P ratio ~13 %, F ~1.5 %, everything else below 1 %.
//   D1 (diagnosis, not a fit): metabolite clearance x 4 with fm rescaled to keep the steady-state ratio. Expected:
//       M Cmax after dose 5 rises to ~30 ng/mL, M AUC0-24 to ~70, and the terminal half-life of M becomes the
//       parent's (formation-limited, ~78 h).
//
// RESULTS (first run on the local Madaros build; the predictions above were NOT edited afterwards).
//   No kernel run preceded the predictions. kappa (the metabolite half-life constant) was then
//   fitted offline: 0.6931 -> 0.833746, which moved CL_M 2.857 -> 3.437 L/h, fm 0.345 -> 0.4196 and the scalar-1
//   formation fraction 1.65 (my hand figure; the closed form gave 2.04) -> 2.61. The early grid was refined from
//   0.25 h to 0.05 h after the first run showed a peak before 1 h (Cmax 88.3 -> 87.3, nothing else moved).
//   row   measured                         outcome   against the pre-registered outcome
//   V1    Cmax 87.3 ng/mL, z +2.37         FAIL      MISSED (predicted PASS at 65): the kernel peaks at 0.75 h
//   V1b   z +3.02                          FAIL      MISSED
//   V1c   6 mg: 52.4 vs 31.0, fold 1.69    FAIL      MISSED
//   V2    Tmax 0.75 h, z -4.2              FAIL      as predicted (the value is earlier than my 1.5-3 h)
//   V3    AUC0-24 729, z +0.02             PASS      as predicted (the value is below my 850-1150)
//   V4    AUC0-72 1316, z -1.06            PASS      as predicted (the value is below my 1750-2150)
//   V5    t1/2 83.6 h, fold 1.11           PASS      as predicted (inside 74-84)
//   V5b   z +2.80                          FAIL      as predicted (forced by S0)
//   V5c   apparent 83.6 h, z +0.71         PASS      as predicted
//   V6    Cmax after dose 5 132.6, z -0.12 PASS      as predicted
//   V6b   ratio 1.52 vs 2.73, fold 0.557   FAIL      MISSED (predicted 2.15, PASS): follows from V1
//   V7    trough 8.23 ng/mL/mg, z -0.27    PASS      as predicted;  V7b 10.43, fold 0.884 PASS as predicted
//   V8    0.939                            PASS      as predicted;  V8b 0.795 FAIL as predicted (0.73)
//   V9    M AUC0-24 75.6, z -0.04          PASS      outcome as predicted, VALUE MISSED (I estimated 30: the first
//                                                    hours, when the parent is high, form more than I allowed for)
//   V9b   M Cmax after dose 5 15.5, z -2.28 FAIL     as predicted
//   V10   4.18 ng/mL/mg, z -0.45           PASS      as predicted
//   V11   PM t1/2 129.4 h, fold 0.886      PASS      as predicted
//   V11b  PM/EM t1/2 1.549, fold 0.795     FAIL      MISSED (predicted 1.64, PASS): the PM half-life is closer to
//                                                    V_ss ln2/CL (ratio 1.095) than the EM one (1.158)
//   V12   0.9995, fold 1.459               FAIL      as predicted: r = 1 is contradicted by the PM metabolite change
//   V13   1.4775, z -1.08                  PASS      as predicted
//   V14   2.00, fold 1.226                 PASS      as predicted (marginal)
//   V15   1.677, fold 0.8003               PASS      MISSED (predicted FAIL at "fold 0.80"; it passes 1.25 by 0.0003)
//   V16   0.207, fold 0.722                FAIL      as predicted
//   V17   0.088 <= 0.18; V18 exact         PASS      as predicted
//   budget 186.2 ng/mL, relative u 0.108; shares CL 86.9 %, M/P ratio 11.4 %, F 1.2 %: as predicted (198, 0.095, 85/13/1.5)
//   D1    M Cmax after dose 5 28.8 (predicted ~30), M t1/2 83.6 h = the parent's (predicted); M AUC0-24 177 against
//         my ~70: MISSED, it overshoots the observed 77.4, so a faster metabolite alone does not reconcile day 1 and day 5.
//   Outcome misses: 6 of 27 rows (V1, V1b, V1c, V6b, V11b, V15); 16 rows pass, 11 fail. The assertions below hold the MEASURED outcomes
//   and bands around the measured numbers; nothing was tuned.
//   D2 (added after the run, a diagnosis, NOT adopted): ka 0.30 /h gives Tmax 4.0 h, Cmax 41.9 ng/mL, ratio 2.08.
//
// =====================================================================================================
// ROUND 2 (everything above is round-1 history and is not edited). Changes asked by the coordinator:
//   (1) ka is FITTED to the pooled Tmax of the single-dose TABLET studies, so Tmax is no longer a validation row
//       and Cmax, accumulation and the day-14 rows are validation. Pool (ari_studies id 7), k = 3: label 4.0 h
//       (3-5 h, tablet, n not given), Kubo 2007 3.6 h (6 mg tablet, healthy Japanese, n not in the abstract),
//       Koller 2020 day 1 5.2 +/- 2.4 h (10 mg tablet, n = 24; the first dose of the 5-day study is a single dose).
//       N = 24 + two unreported. Li 2025 (median 3 h, n = 30) is an orally disintegrating tablet and is NOT pooled.
//       Pooled 4.267 h; SE within = sqrt(sum SE^2)/k = 0.163 h; SE between = 0.833/sqrt 3 = 0.481 h; u = 0.481 h.
//   (2) The observed accumulation 2.73 is Koller's Cmax after the FIFTH daily dose over Cmax after the first
//       (138.0/50.6, ratio of means; day 5, not steady state, not AUC). The round-1 row computed exactly that
//       quantity (max over the fifth interval of the superposed curve / single-dose Cmax), so the row was the
//       right quantity. Printed beside it in round 2: the model's steady-state Cmax ratio, trough ratio and the
//       AUC accumulation AUC(0-inf)/AUC(0-24), which no source I read reports.
//   (3) One labelled diagnostic of the enzyme assignment of the formation route (S6d), not adopted.
//
// ROUND 2 PREDICTIONS, written before any round-2 kernel run. They are interpolated from the round-1 scan that I
// had already seen (ka 0.30: Tmax 4.00 h, Cmax 41.86, Cmax after dose 5 87.19, ss Cmax 123.69, ss trough 85.19, AM
// trough 127.39; ka 0.20: 5.77 h, 35.61, 81.53, 118.04, 87.43, 129.84; all per 10 mg), so they are not blind.
//   ka fitted                        0.28 /h (0.26-0.29)
//   single-dose Cmax (ng/mL)         5 mg 20.5; 6 mg 24.5; 10 mg 40.9 (40-42); 15 mg 61.4; 20 mg 81.8; 30 mg 122.7
//   V1  Cmax 10 mg vs 50.6 +/- 15.5  z -0.63   PASS         V1b vs 48 +/- 13 (ODT)  z -0.55  PASS
//   V1c Cmax 6 mg vs 31.0            fold 0.79 PASS
//   V3  AUC0-24 10 mg                677 (665-690)  vs 724.9 +/- 236.5   z -0.2   PASS
//   V4  AUC0-72 10 mg                1286 (1275-1300) vs 1745 +/- 405    z -1.13  PASS
//   V5/V5b/V5c half-life             83.6 h unchanged (ka does not enter the terminal phase): PASS / FAIL / PASS
//   V6  Cmax after dose 5            86.3 (85-87.5)  vs 138.0 +/- 45.9   z -1.13  PASS
//   V6b Cmax dose 5 / dose 1         2.11 (2.08-2.15) vs 2.73            fold 0.77 PASS at 1.5
//   steady state per 10 mg/day       P Cmax 122.8 (121-124); P trough 85.5 (85-86.5); AM trough 127.7 (127-129)
//       model accumulation at steady state: Cmax,ss/Cmax,1 3.00; AUC(0-inf)/AUC(0-24) 3.70
//   V7  P trough,ss per mg/day       8.55 vs 9.0 +/- 2.9  PASS;   V7b unchanged 10.43 PASS
//   V8  P trough day 14 / ss         0.939 unchanged PASS;  V8b M 0.795 unchanged FAIL
//   V9  M AUC0-24 day 1              ~70 (60-76) vs 77.4 +/- 43.9 PASS;   V9b M Cmax after dose 5 ~15 (14-16) FAIL
//   PM rows, what-ifs                unchanged in outcome (closed forms do not contain ka); PM half-life 129.4 h
//   budget (15 mg/day)               AM trough 191.5 ng/mL, relative u 0.108; shares CL ~86.5 %, M/P ~11.4 %, F ~1.2 %,
//                                    pooled Tmax (through ka) ~0.2 %
//   S6d enzyme assignment (closed form, hand): PM/EM metabolite exposure: formation entirely CYP3A4 1.68, equal
//       share 1.00, entirely CYP2D6 0 (and infeasible: it needs phi_D = fm/f2D6 = 1.04 > 1); observed 0.685 lies
//       between "equal" and "entirely CYP2D6" and is nearest to "equal" in log distance. PM/EM active moiety: 1.68 /
//       1.48 / 1.18 against 1.585. The PM/EM half-life ratio of the parent is 1.549 in all three (the parent's
//       clearance does not depend on which enzyme makes the metabolite), so it cannot discriminate.
//   Expected remaining failures: V5b, V8b, V9b, V11b, V12, V16 (six rows).
// =====================================================================================================
// ROUND 2 RESULTS (predictions above not edited). ka fitted offline: 0.284844 /h (predicted 0.28), kernel Tmax 4.2667 h.
//   Cmax 10 mg 41.02 (predicted 40.9): V1 z -0.62 PASS, V1b z -0.54 PASS, V1c 24.6 vs 31.0 fold 0.794 PASS: all as predicted.
//   AUC0-24 678.3 (677), AUC0-72 1287.0 (1286), Cmax after dose 5 86.46 (86.3), ratio 2.108 (2.11): PASS, as predicted.
//   steady state per 10 mg/day: P Cmax 122.82 (122.8), P trough 85.42 (85.5), AM trough 127.64 (127.7): inside the ranges.
//   accumulation on the model: Cmax,ss/Cmax,1 2.994 (3.00), AUC(0-inf)/AUC(0-24) 3.689 (3.70), trough,ss/C(24 h) 4.96.
//   V8 0.940, V8b 0.794 FAIL, V9 66.7 PASS, V9b 15.4 FAIL, half-life and PM rows and what-ifs unchanged: as predicted.
//   budget: 191.46 ng/mL (191.5), relative u 0.1056 (0.108), CL 86.8 %, M/P 11.4 %, F 1.2 %, pooled Tmax 0.14 % (0.2 %).
//   S6d: 1.678 / 0.999 / 0 (infeasible, phi_D 1.038); nearest to the observed 0.685: equal share. As predicted.
//   Every round-2 outcome prediction was hit. 26 validation rows: 20 pass, 6 fail (V5b, V8b, V9b, V11b, V12, V16).
//
// COMPILER WORKAROUNDS (not fixed, recorded): every record fit and every kernel run is called from main through
// small functions taking record references (Madaros segfaulted on a main that held two records and five
// [f64; 18] arrays: measured in a scratch program for this drug); big arrays live in the run function; a guard
// row compares the kernel AUC with the closed form.

use darwin_pbpk::circ28::*
use darwin_pbpk::circ28_kp::*
use darwin_pbpk::circ28_drug::*
use darwin_pbpk::circ28_metab::*
use darwin_pbpk::circ28_drug_aripiprazole::*
use math::pure::{exp}

fn at_fold(tag: string, pred: f64, obs: f64, fold: f64, expect_pass: i32) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic {
    let r = pred / obs
    var ok: i32 = 0
    if r <= fold && r >= 1.0 / fold { ok = 1 }
    print("  "); print(tag); print("  pred "); print(pred); print("  obs "); print(obs); print("  fold "); print(r)
    if ok == 1 { print("  [pass]") } else { print("  [fail]") }
    if ok != expect_pass {
        println("  ** differs from the pre-registered outcome **")
        return 1
    }
    println("")
    return 0
}

fn at_z(tag: string, pred: f64, obs: f64, sd: f64, expect_pass: i32) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic {
    let z = (pred - obs) / sd
    var ok: i32 = 0
    if z <= 2.0 && z >= 0.0 - 2.0 { ok = 1 }
    print("  "); print(tag); print("  pred "); print(pred); print("  obs "); print(obs); print("  SD "); print(sd); print("  z "); print(z)
    if ok == 1 { print("  [pass]") } else { print("  [fail]") }
    if ok != expect_pass {
        println("  ** differs from the pre-registered outcome **")
        return 1
    }
    println("")
    return 0
}

fn at_band(tag: string, v: f64, lo: f64, hi: f64) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic {
    if v >= lo && v <= hi { return 0 }
    print("  [FAIL] "); print(tag); print(" = "); print(v); print(" outside ["); print(lo); print(", "); print(hi); println("]")
    return 1
}

fn at_rel(tag: string, got: f64, want: f64, tol: f64) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic {
    var d = got - want
    if d < 0.0 { d = 0.0 - d }
    d = d / want
    print("  "); print(tag); print("  got "); print(got); print("  want "); print(want); print("  rel "); println(d)
    if d > tol {
        println("  [FAIL] above tolerance")
        return 1
    }
    return 0
}

fn at_pool(tag: string, id: i32) with IO, Mut, Div, Panic {
    print("  "); print(tag); print("  mean "); print(ari_obs(id, 0)); print("  between-study SD "); print(ari_obs(id, 1)); print("  u "); println(ari_obs(id, 2))
}

// closed forms of the records (one small frame each)
fn at_fm(dp: &Circ28Drug, dm: &Circ28Drug) -> f64 with Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    return ari_fm(circ28_drug_theta(dp), circ28_drug_theta(dm), ari_obs(4, 0))
}
fn at_f2d6(dp: &Circ28Drug) -> f64 with Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    return ari_f2d6(circ28_drug_theta(dp), ari_obs(3, 0))
}
// which: 0 CL, 1 V_ss, 2 CL/(1-Eh), 3 Eh, 4 fa, 5 fa/clf (AUCinf per mg oral, h/L)
fn at_cf(d: &Circ28Drug, which: i32) -> f64 with Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    let th = circ28_drug_theta(d)
    if which == 0 { return ari_cl(th) }
    if which == 1 { return ari_vss(th) }
    if which == 2 { return ari_clf(th) }
    if which == 3 { return ari_eh(th) }
    if which == 4 { return th[CD_FA] }
    return th[CD_FA] / ari_clf(th)
}
// Oral AUC ratio scenario/base of the parent (which = 0), of the metabolite (1), of the active moiety (2);
// 3: V_ss ln2/CL of the scenario. gm = share of the metabolite's clearance scaled with srest (0 = unchanged).
fn at_scen(dp: &Circ28Drug, dm: &Circ28Drug, f: f64, r: f64, s2d6: f64, srest: f64, which: i32) -> f64 with Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    let thp = circ28_drug_theta(dp)
    let thm = circ28_drug_theta(dm)
    let sc = ari_scenario(thp, f, r, s2d6, srest)
    let rp = ari_clf(thp) / ari_clf(sc)
    if which == 0 { return rp }
    let q0 = ari_ratio_cf(thp, thm)
    let q1 = ari_ratio_cf(sc, thm)
    let rm = rp * q1 / q0
    if which == 1 { return rm }
    if which == 2 { return (rp + q0 * rm) / (1.0 + q0) }
    return 0.6931471805599453 * ari_vss(sc) / ari_cl(sc)
}
fn at_rr1(dp: &Circ28Drug, dm: &Circ28Drug, which: i32) -> f64 with Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    let tm1 = ari_fit_m(circ28_drug_theta(dm), 1.0, ari_obs(5, 0), ari_m_kappa())
    if which == 0 { return ari_vss(tm1) }
    if which == 1 { return ari_cl(tm1) }
    var tp = circ28_drug_theta(dp)
    return ari_fm(tp, tm1, ari_obs(4, 0))
}

// Enzyme assignment of the formation route (diagnostic S6d). which_case 0: formation entirely by the non-2D6
// route (CYP3A4); 1: equal share (r = 1); 2: entirely CYP2D6. out: 0 phi_D, 1 phi_A, 2 PM/EM metabolite exposure,
// 3 PM/EM parent exposure (the active moiety is formed from it in main), 4 PM/EM V_ss ln2/CL of the parent.
fn at_enz(dp: &Circ28Drug, dm: &Circ28Drug, f: f64, which_case: i32, out: &![f64; 5]) with Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    let thp = circ28_drug_theta(dp)
    let thm = circ28_drug_theta(dm)
    let fm = thp[CD_CLFORM] / (thp[CD_CLINT] + thp[CD_CLFORM])
    var phid = fm
    var phia = fm
    if which_case == 0 {
        phid = 0.0
        phia = fm / (1.0 - f)
    }
    if which_case == 2 {
        phid = fm / f
        phia = 0.0
    }
    let sc = ari_scenario_phi(thp, f, phid, phia, 0.0, 1.0)
    let rp = ari_clf(thp) / ari_clf(sc)
    let q0 = ari_ratio_cf(thp, thm)
    let q1 = ari_ratio_cf(sc, thm)
    let rm = rp * q1 / q0
    let hr = (ari_vss(sc) / ari_cl(sc)) / (ari_vss(thp) / ari_cl(thp))
    (*out)[0] = phid
    (*out)[1] = phia
    (*out)[2] = rm
    (*out)[3] = rp
    (*out)[4] = hr
}

// One coupled oral run. mode 0 EM; 1 PM (CYP2D6 part removed, r = 1); 2 diagnostic D1: metabolite hepatic
// intrinsic clearance x 4 and the parent's fm rescaled so that the closed-form M/P ratio is unchanged.
fn at_run(dp: &Circ28Drug, dm: &Circ28Drug, dose: f64, mode: i32, f: f64, tail: f64, res: &![f64; 40]) with Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var thp = circ28_drug_theta(dp)
    var thm = circ28_drug_theta(dm)
    if mode == 1 {
        thp = ari_scenario(thp, f, ari_r_base(), 0.0, 1.0)
    }
    if mode == 2 {
        let q0 = ari_ratio_cf(thp, thm)
        thm[CD_CLINT] = 4.0 * thm[CD_CLINT]
        let q1 = ari_ratio_cf(thp, thm)
        let tot = thp[CD_CLINT] + thp[CD_CLFORM]
        let fm = (thp[CD_CLFORM] / tot) * q0 / q1
        thp[CD_CLFORM] = fm * tot
        thp[CD_CLINT] = (1.0 - fm) * tot
    }
    if mode == 3 {   // unused since round 2 (kept for a manual re-run of the round-1 base)
        thp[CD_KA] = ari_p_ka_poppk()
    }
    var wlo = 300.0
    var whi = 600.0
    if mode == 1 {
        wlo = 600.0
        whi = 1200.0
    }
    ari_run_th(thp, thm, 1, dose, 0.0, tail, wlo, whi, 1200.0, 1680.0, res)
}

fn at_show(tag: string, r: &[f64; 40]) with IO, Mut, Div, Panic {
    print(tag); print(": P Cmax "); print(1000.0 * (*r)[0]); print(" ng/mL  Tmax "); print((*r)[1]); print(" h  AUCinf "); print(1000.0 * (*r)[2]); print("  t1/2 "); println((*r)[3])
    print("      M Cmax "); print(1000.0 * (*r)[6]); print("  Tmax "); print((*r)[7]); print("  AUCinf "); print(1000.0 * (*r)[8]); print("  t1/2 "); println((*r)[9])
    print("      ss: P Cmax "); print(1000.0 * (*r)[16]); print(" (Tmax "); print((*r)[17]); print(")  trough "); print(1000.0 * (*r)[18]); print("   M Cmax "); print(1000.0 * (*r)[19]); print("  trough "); print(1000.0 * (*r)[20])
    print("   AM Cmax "); print(1000.0 * (*r)[21]); print("  trough "); println(1000.0 * (*r)[22])
    print("      balance P "); print((*r)[12]); print("  M "); print((*r)[13]); print("  grid ok "); println((*r)[14])
}

fn at_budget(dp: &Circ28Drug, dm: &Circ28Drug) -> i32 with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var fails: i32 = 0
    let b = ari_budget(dp, dm, 15.0)
    let am = 1000.0 * b.y0[0]
    let u = 1000.0 * cd_sqrt(b.var_am)
    print("S7 uncertainty budget with refit, 15 mg once daily at steady state ("); print(b.runs); println(" coupled runs, forward differences)")
    print("  active-moiety trough "); print(am); print(" ng/mL  u "); print(u); print("  relative "); println(u / am)
    print("  parent trough "); print(1000.0 * b.y0[1]); print("  u "); print(1000.0 * cd_sqrt(b.var_p)); print("   metabolite trough "); print(1000.0 * b.y0[2]); print("  u "); println(1000.0 * cd_sqrt(b.var_m))
    print("  parent AUCinf per 15 mg "); print(1000.0 * b.y0[3]); print(" ng h/mL  u "); println(1000.0 * cd_sqrt(b.var_auc))
    println("  input               u(input)     share of var(active-moiety trough) %")
    var i: i32 = 0
    while i < 13 {
        print("  "); print(ari_input_name(i)); print("  "); print(b.u[i]); print("   "); println(100.0 * b.contrib_am[i] / b.var_am)
        i = i + 1
    }
    fails = fails + at_band("budget: AM trough (ng/mL), hand prediction 198", am, 150.0, 250.0)
    fails = fails + at_band("budget: relative u, hand prediction 0.095", u / am, 0.06, 0.14)
    fails = fails + at_band("budget: share of the pooled CL (%), hand prediction 85", 100.0 * b.contrib_am[0] / b.var_am, 60.0, 95.0)
    return fails
}

fn main() with IO, Mut, Div, Panic, Epistemic {
    var fails: i32 = 0
    // WORKAROUND: both records are created before ANY floating-point operation in main. On Madaros (local
    // and committed) a float computed or printed in main before circ28_drug_new() makes the later
    // circ28_drug_theta() segfault (minimal reproducer in the report); lean_single is not affected.
    var dm = circ28_drug_new()
    var dp = circ28_drug_new()
    let ln2 = 0.6931471805599453
    // ---- S0: pooled observables and the input-consistency check, before any run
    println("S0 pooled observables (mean, between-study SD, u = max(pooled SE, SD/sqrt k))")
    at_pool("F                      k=2", 0)
    at_pool("CL (L/h, 73 kg)        k=4", 1)
    at_pool("V_ss (L)               k=1", 2)
    at_pool("PM/EM parent exposure  k=3", 3)
    at_pool("M/P ratio at ss (EM)   k=5", 4)
    at_pool("t1/2 M (h)             k=2", 5)
    at_pool("t1/2 P (h) [validation] k=5", 6)
    at_pool("Tmax P (h) [validation] k=3", 7)
    at_pool("PM/EM active moiety [v] k=4", 8)
    at_pool("PM/EM metabolite [v]    k=2", 9)
    let chk = ari_obs(2, 0) * ln2 / ari_obs(1, 0)
    println("S0 INPUT-CONSISTENCY CHECK: V_ss ln2 / CL against the terminal half-life")
    print("  V_ss ln2/CL (pooled CL) = "); print(chk); print(" h;  with the IV clearance alone (0.7 mL/min/kg) = "); println(ari_obs(2, 0) * ln2 / (0.7 * 60.0 / 1000.0 * ari_weight()))
    print("  terminal half-life: label 75 h (ratio "); print(chk / 75.0); print(");  pooled "); print(ari_obs(6, 0)); print(" h (ratio "); print(chk / ari_obs(6, 0)); println(")")
    println("  => INCONSISTENT against the pooled half-life (a terminal half-life cannot be below V_ss ln2/CL); no room")
    println("     for a distribution phase against the label. V_z bounds on V_ss from the oral studies (L):")
    print("     Mallikaarjun study 1 "); print(3.45 * ari_obs(0, 0) * 57.5 / ln2); print("  study 2 "); print(4.0 * ari_obs(0, 0) * 59.0 / ln2)
    print("  Koller "); print(6.0 * ari_weight() * ari_obs(0, 0)); print("  label CL x 75 h "); println(0.7 * 60.0 / 1000.0 * ari_weight() * 75.0 / ln2)
    fails = fails + at_band("S0 V_ss ln2/CL (h)", chk, 71.0, 73.5)
    fails = fails + at_band("S0 ratio to the pooled half-life (asserted as measured: > 1)", chk / ari_obs(6, 0), 1.08, 1.18)

    // ---- records (each step called from main)
    ari_measured_p(&!dp)
    ari_fit_record_p1(&!dp)
    ari_measured_m(&!dm)
    ari_fit_record_m(&!dm, circ28_drug_value(&dp, CD_KPSC))
    let fm = at_fm(&dp, &dm)
    ari_fit_record_p2(&!dp, fm)
    let f = at_f2d6(&dp)
    println("S1 records: P then M (value, status)")
    var i: i32 = 0
    while i < 18 {
        print("  P "); print(i); print(" "); print(circ28_drug_value(&dp, i)); print("  status "); print(dp.status[i])
        print("   |  M "); print(circ28_drug_value(&dm, i)); print("  status "); println(dm.status[i])
        i = i + 1
    }
    print("  fm = "); print(fm); print("   f2D6 = "); print(f); print("   Eh = "); println(at_cf(&dp, 3))
    println("S1 the fits reproduce their observables (NOT validations)")
    fails = fails + at_rel("V_ss P (L)", at_cf(&dp, 1), ari_obs(2, 0), 1.0e-9)
    fails = fails + at_rel("CL P (L/h)", at_cf(&dp, 0), ari_obs(1, 0), 1.0e-9)
    fails = fails + at_rel("F = fa (1 - Eh)", at_cf(&dp, 4) * (1.0 - at_cf(&dp, 3)), ari_obs(0, 0), 1.0e-9)
    fails = fails + at_rel("(CL/F)_EM/(CL/F)_PM (closed form)", at_scen(&dp, &dm, f, 1.0, 0.0, 1.0, 0), ari_obs(3, 0), 1.0e-9)
    fails = fails + at_band("fm", fm, 0.40, 0.44)
    fails = fails + at_band("f2D6", f, 0.39, 0.42)
    println("  Rodgers-Rowland with scalar 1 for the metabolite (the declared prediction), tested:")
    print("    V_ss,M "); print(at_rr1(&dp, &dm, 0)); print(" L   CL_M "); print(at_rr1(&dp, &dm, 1)); print(" L/h   formation fraction needed "); print(at_rr1(&dp, &dm, 2)); println("  (> 1: infeasible)")
    fails = fails + at_band("RR scalar-1 formation fraction (must exceed 1 for the statement above)", at_rr1(&dp, &dm, 2), 2.4, 2.8)
    print("    adopted instead (ASSUMPTION): Kp scalar of M = Kp scalar of P -> V_ss,M "); print(at_cf(&dm, 1)); print(" L, CL_M "); print(at_cf(&dm, 0)); println(" L/h")

    // ---- S2: EM, oral 10 mg
    var em: [f64; 40] = [0.0; 40]
    at_run(&dp, &dm, 10.0, 0, f, 8.0, &!em)
    at_show("S2 oral 10 mg EM", &em)
    fails = fails + at_band("balance P", em[12], 0.0, 1.0e-9)
    fails = fails + at_band("balance M", em[13], 0.0, 1.0e-9)
    fails = fails + at_band("grid ok", em[14], 0.5, 1.5)
    fails = fails + at_rel("GUARD kernel AUCinf P vs closed form fa D/(CL/(1-Eh))", em[2], 10.0 * at_cf(&dp, 5), 2.0e-3)
    fails = fails + at_rel("M/P AUCinf ratio (kernel) = pooled 0.417 [fitted]", em[8] / em[2], ari_obs(4, 0), 1.0e-2)
    fails = fails + at_rel("terminal t1/2 M (kernel, 1200-1680 h) = pooled 100.65 h [fitted]", em[9], ari_obs(5, 0), 2.0e-2)
    println("V validation, predicted vs observed (criteria and expectations fixed before the runs: header)")
    fails = fails + at_z("V1  Cmax 10 mg (ng/mL), Koller 50.6 +/- 15.5 (c)     ", 1000.0 * em[0], 50.6, 15.5, 1)
    fails = fails + at_z("V1b Cmax 10 mg, Li 48 +/- 13 (ODT)                   ", 1000.0 * em[0], 48.0, 13.0, 1)
    fails = fails + at_fold("V1c Cmax 6 mg, Kubo 31.0                             ", 600.0 * em[0], 31.0, 1.5, 1)
    fails = fails + at_rel("Tmax (h) = pooled 4.267 h of the tablet studies [FITTED in round 2: ka]", em[1], ari_obs(7, 0), 5.0e-3)
    fails = fails + at_z("V3  AUC0-24 10 mg (ng h/mL), Koller 724.9 +/- 236.5 (c)", 1000.0 * em[4], 724.9, 236.5, 1)
    fails = fails + at_z("V4  AUC0-72 10 mg, Li 1745 +/- 405                   ", 1000.0 * em[5], 1745.0, 405.0, 1)
    fails = fails + at_fold("V5  terminal t1/2 P (h), label 75                    ", em[3], 75.0, 1.5, 1)
    fails = fails + at_z("V5b terminal t1/2 P vs pooled 63.7, SD 7.1           ", em[3], ari_obs(6, 0), ari_obs(6, 1), 0)
    fails = fails + at_z("V5c apparent t1/2 P 96-240 h, Koller 66.1 +/- 24.6   ", em[27], 66.1, 24.6, 1)
    fails = fails + at_z("V6  Cmax after dose 5, Koller 138.0 +/- 45.9 (c)     ", 1000.0 * em[23], 138.0, 45.9, 1)
    fails = fails + at_fold("V6b Cmax dose 5 / dose 1, Koller 2.73                ", em[23] / em[0], 138.0 / 50.6, 1.5, 1)
    fails = fails + at_z("V7  P trough,ss per mg/day, Suzuki 9.0 +/- 2.9       ", 100.0 * em[18], 9.0, 2.9, 1)
    fails = fails + at_fold("V7b P average,ss per mg/day, Hendset 11.8            ", 1000.0 * at_cf(&dp, 5) / 24.0, 26.3 * ari_p_mw() / 1000.0, 1.5, 1)
    var ok8: i32 = 0
    if em[25] >= 0.90 { ok8 = 1 }
    print("  V8  P trough day 14 / steady state "); print(em[25]); if ok8 == 1 { println("  [pass]") } else { println("  [fail]") }
    if ok8 != 1 { fails = fails + 1 }
    var ok8b: i32 = 0
    if em[26] >= 0.90 { ok8b = 1 }
    print("  V8b M trough day 14 / steady state "); print(em[26]); if ok8b == 1 { println("  [pass]") } else { println("  [fail]") }
    if ok8b != 0 { fails = fails + 1 }
    fails = fails + at_z("V9  M AUC0-24 day 1 (ng h/mL), Koller 77.4 +/- 43.9  ", 1000.0 * em[10], 77.4, 43.9, 1)
    fails = fails + at_z("V9b M Cmax after dose 5, Koller 34.9 +/- 8.5 (c)     ", 1000.0 * em[24], 34.9, 8.5, 0)
    fails = fails + at_z("V10 M trough,ss per mg/day, Suzuki 4.9 +/- 1.6 (c)   ", 100.0 * em[20], 4.9, 1.6, 1)
    print("  apparent t1/2 M over 336-576 h (what a 2-3 week sampling would see): "); print(em[28]); println(" h")
    // dose linearity: the kernel is linear; one more run at 30 mg against 6 x a 5 mg scaling of the 10 mg run
    var hi: [f64; 40] = [0.0; 40]
    at_run(&dp, &dm, 30.0, 0, f, 8.0, &!hi)
    fails = fails + at_rel("V18 dose linearity: Cmax(30 mg)/Cmax(10 mg) = 3", hi[0] / em[0], 3.0, 1.0e-9)
    fails = fails + at_rel("V18 dose linearity: AM trough,ss(30)/(10) = 3", hi[22] / em[22], 3.0, 1.0e-9)
    print("  V17 unabsorbed fraction 1 - fa = "); print(1.0 - at_cf(&dp, 4)); println("  against <= 0.18 (unchanged in faeces, label)")
    fails = fails + at_band("V17 1 - fa (bound 0.18; hand 0.088)", 1.0 - at_cf(&dp, 4), 0.0, 0.18)
    // bands around the measured outcomes of the rows that failed (asserted as measured, not tuned)
    fails = fails + at_band("terminal t1/2 P (h): measured 83.6, hand prediction 78 (74-84)", em[3], 82.5, 84.6)
    fails = fails + at_band("M Cmax after dose 5 (ng/mL): round 2 measured 15.4 (predicted 14-16)", 1000.0 * em[24], 14.9, 15.9)
    fails = fails + at_band("ROUND 2 Cmax 10 mg (ng/mL): predicted 40-42", 1000.0 * em[0], 40.0, 42.0)
    fails = fails + at_band("ROUND 2 Cmax dose 5 / dose 1: predicted 2.08-2.15", em[23] / em[0], 2.08, 2.15)
    fails = fails + at_band("ROUND 2 P Cmax,ss per 10 mg: predicted 121-124", 1000.0 * em[16], 121.0, 124.0)
    fails = fails + at_band("ROUND 2 P trough,ss per 10 mg: predicted 85-86.5", 1000.0 * em[18], 85.0, 86.5)
    fails = fails + at_band("ROUND 2 AM trough,ss per 10 mg: predicted 127-129", 1000.0 * em[22], 127.0, 129.0)
    fails = fails + at_band("M trough day 14 / ss: measured 0.795, hand prediction 0.73", em[26], 0.78, 0.81)
    // convergence of the large tail steps: the same run with 2 h instead of 8 h steps after 240 h
    var fine: [f64; 40] = [0.0; 40]
    at_run(&dp, &dm, 10.0, 0, f, 2.0, &!fine)
    fails = fails + at_rel("CONVERGENCE tail step 8 h vs 2 h: terminal t1/2 P", em[3], fine[3], 1.0e-3)
    fails = fails + at_rel("CONVERGENCE tail step 8 h vs 2 h: AM trough,ss", em[22], fine[22], 1.0e-3)
    fails = fails + at_rel("CONVERGENCE tail step 8 h vs 2 h: P Cmax,ss", em[16], fine[16], 1.0e-3)

    // ---- S4: poor metaboliser
    var pm: [f64; 40] = [0.0; 40]
    at_run(&dp, &dm, 10.0, 1, f, 8.0, &!pm)
    at_show("S4 oral 10 mg PM (CYP2D6 part removed, r = 1)", &pm)
    fails = fails + at_rel("GUARD PM/EM parent AUCinf (kernel) = pooled 1.677 [fitted]", pm[2] / em[2], ari_obs(3, 0), 5.0e-3)
    fails = fails + at_fold("V11 PM terminal t1/2 P (h), label 146                ", pm[3], 146.0, 1.5, 1)
    fails = fails + at_fold("V11b PM/EM t1/2 ratio, label 146/75                  ", pm[3] / em[3], 146.0 / 75.0, 1.25, 0)
    fails = fails + at_fold("V12 PM/EM metabolite exposure, pooled 0.685 (r = 1)  ", pm[8] / em[8], ari_obs(9, 0), 1.25, 0)
    fails = fails + at_z("V13 PM/EM active moiety AUC, pooled 1.585, SD 0.100  ", (pm[2] + pm[8]) / (em[2] + em[8]), ari_obs(8, 0), ari_obs(8, 1), 1)
    print("  PM steady state per mg/day: P trough "); print(100.0 * pm[18]); print("  AM trough "); print(100.0 * pm[22]); print("  (Hendset PM medians: P 20.4, sum 24.2 ng/mL/mg);  M t1/2 in PM "); println(pm[9])
    fails = fails + at_band("PM terminal t1/2 P (h): measured 129.4, hand prediction 128 (120-136)", pm[3], 127.5, 131.5)
    fails = fails + at_band("PM/EM t1/2 ratio: measured 1.549, hand prediction 1.64 MISSED (fold 0.795 against 146/75)", pm[3] / em[3], 1.53, 1.57)
    fails = fails + at_band("PM/EM metabolite exposure (r = 1): measured 0.9995", pm[8] / em[8], 0.99, 1.01)

    // ---- S5: what-ifs on the hepatic factors (closed form; LABELLED, not mechanistic)
    println("S5 interaction what-ifs (oral AUC ratio of the parent; closed form)")
    fails = fails + at_fold("V14 ketoconazole: non-2D6 x 0.16, obs 1.63           ", at_scen(&dp, &dm, f, 1.0, 1.0, 0.16, 0), 1.63, 1.25, 1)
    fails = fails + at_fold("V15 quinidine: 2D6 x 0, obs 2.095                    ", at_scen(&dp, &dm, f, 1.0, 0.0, 1.0, 0), 0.5 * (2.12 + 2.07), 1.25, 1)
    fails = fails + at_fold("V16 carbamazepine: non-2D6 x 7.5, obs 0.287          ", at_scen(&dp, &dm, f, 1.0, 1.0, 7.5, 0), (0.30 + 0.27 + 0.29) / 3.0, 1.25, 0)
    print("  ketoconazole with complete inhibition of the non-2D6 part (upper bound): "); println(at_scen(&dp, &dm, f, 1.0, 1.0, 0.0, 0))
    fails = fails + at_band("ketoconazole what-if (closed form 2.00)", at_scen(&dp, &dm, f, 1.0, 1.0, 0.16, 0), 1.98, 2.02)
    fails = fails + at_band("quinidine what-if (closed form 1.677; fold 0.8003: passes 1.25 by 0.0003, predicted FAIL)", at_scen(&dp, &dm, f, 1.0, 0.0, 1.0, 0), 1.67, 1.685)
    fails = fails + at_band("carbamazepine what-if (closed form 0.207)", at_scen(&dp, &dm, f, 1.0, 1.0, 7.5, 0), 0.203, 0.211)
    print("  non-2D6 factor that gives 1.63: "); println((1.0 / 1.63 - f) / (1.0 - f))
    print("  non-2D6 factor that gives 0.287: "); println((1.0 / 0.2867 - f) / (1.0 - f))
    print("  f2D6 that quinidine's 2.095 would need (if inhibition were complete): "); println(1.0 - 1.0 / 2.095)
    println("  metabolite under the what-ifs, formation only (r = 1; the metabolite's own enzymes are not sourced):")
    print("    ketoconazole "); print(at_scen(&dp, &dm, f, 1.0, 1.0, 0.16, 1)); print(" (obs 1.77)   quinidine "); print(at_scen(&dp, &dm, f, 1.0, 0.0, 1.0, 1)); print(" (obs 0.65-0.68)   carbamazepine "); print(at_scen(&dp, &dm, f, 1.0, 1.0, 7.5, 1)); println(" (obs 0.29-0.31)")

    // ---- S6: diagnoses (not fits)
    println("S6a diagnosis: r = phi_A/phi_D (share of dehydrogenation in the non-2D6 clearance over that in CYP2D6)")
    var jr: i32 = 0
    while jr < 5 {
        var rv = 1.0
        if jr == 1 { rv = 0.75 }
        if jr == 2 { rv = 0.56 }
        if jr == 3 { rv = 0.4 }
        if jr == 4 { rv = 0.0 }
        print("  r "); print(rv); print("  PM/EM metabolite "); print(at_scen(&dp, &dm, f, rv, 0.0, 1.0, 1)); print("  PM/EM active moiety "); println(at_scen(&dp, &dm, f, rv, 0.0, 1.0, 2))
        jr = jr + 1
    }
    println("  (observed: metabolite 0.685, active moiety 1.585)")
    var d1: [f64; 40] = [0.0; 40]
    at_run(&dp, &dm, 10.0, 2, f, 8.0, &!d1)
    at_show("S6b diagnosis D1: metabolite clearance x 4, fm rescaled (10 mg)", &d1)
    print("  D1: M AUC0-24 "); print(1000.0 * d1[10]); print(" (obs 77.4)  M Cmax after dose 5 "); print(1000.0 * d1[24]); print(" (obs 34.9)  M trough day 14/ss "); print(d1[26]); print("  M/P AUCinf "); println(d1[8] / d1[2])
    print("  base: M AUC0-24 "); print(1000.0 * em[10]); print("  M Cmax after dose 5 "); print(1000.0 * em[24]); print("  M trough day 14/ss "); println(em[26])

    println("S6c D2 (round-1 base, ka 1.67 /h of the FDA review): Cmax 87.3 ng/mL, Tmax 0.75 h, ratio 1.52; recorded in round 1, not re-run")
    println("S6d diagnosis (LABELLED, not adopted): which enzyme forms the metabolite. PM = CYP2D6 part removed.")
    println("    case                      phi_D     phi_A     PM/EM metabolite (obs 0.685)   PM/EM active moiety (obs 1.585)   PM/EM V_ss ln2/CL of P")
    var je: i32 = 0
    var best: i32 = 0 - 1
    var bestd = 1.0e9
    while je < 3 {
        var eo: [f64; 5] = [0.0; 5]
        at_enz(&dp, &dm, f, je, &!eo)
        // lean_single returned 1.4886 instead of 1.4775 for the active moiety when it was computed inside at_enz
        // (q0 read back wrong there); it is therefore computed here in main from the parent ratio, the kernel M/P
        // ratio and the metabolite ratio, and a GUARD row compares the equal-share case with the at_scen value
        eo[3] = (eo[3] + (em[8] / em[2]) * eo[2]) / (1.0 + em[8] / em[2])
        if je == 1 { fails = fails + at_rel("GUARD S6d equal-share active moiety = at_scen value", eo[3], at_scen(&dp, &dm, f, 1.0, 0.0, 1.0, 2), 1.0e-5) }
        if je == 0 { print("    entirely non-2D6 (CYP3A4)  ") }
        if je == 1 { print("    equal share (base, r = 1)  ") }
        if je == 2 { print("    entirely CYP2D6            ") }
        print(eo[0]); print("  "); print(eo[1]); print("  "); print(eo[2]); print("   "); print(eo[3]); print("   "); print(eo[4])
        if eo[0] > 1.0 || eo[1] > 1.0 { print("   INFEASIBLE (a share above 1)") }
        println("")
        var dd = eo[2] - ari_obs(9, 0)
        if dd < 0.0 { dd = 0.0 - dd }
        if dd < bestd {
            bestd = dd
            best = je
        }
        je = je + 1
    }
    print("  the PM metabolite change (-31.5 %) is nearest to case "); print(best); println(" (0 CYP3A4 only, 1 equal share, 2 CYP2D6 only); it lies between 1 and 2")
    println("  the PM/EM half-life ratio of the parent is the same in all three cases: it cannot discriminate")
    fails = fails + at_band("S6d favoured case (hand prediction: 1, equal share)", best as f64, 0.5, 1.5)
    println("S6e accumulation, all computed on the model (10 mg once daily); the observed 2.73 is Cmax after dose 5 / Cmax after dose 1")
    print("  Cmax dose 5 / dose 1 "); print(em[23] / em[0]); print("   Cmax,ss / Cmax,1 "); print(em[16] / em[0]); print("   trough,ss / C(24 h) "); print(em[18] / em[33]); print("   AUC(0-inf)/AUC(0-24) "); println(em[2] / em[4])
    print("  one-compartment value for a 24 h interval and the terminal half-life: "); println(1.0 / (1.0 - exp(0.0 - 0.6931471805599453 * 24.0 / em[3])))
    // ---- S7: budget
    fails = fails + at_budget(&dp, &dm)
    if fails == 0 { println("CIRC28_DRUG_ARIPIPRAZOLE_PASS") } else { print("FAILS "); println(fails) }
}
